cted': 'No exception; the existing RRset now contains both A records (192.0.2.10 and 192.0.2.11).', 'description': 'Adding a second record with the same name and type should add to the existing RRset rather than creating a new one.'}]}, {'group': 'Replace Existing SOA', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'r', 'value': 'initialSOA = new SOARecord(Name.fromString("example.com."), DClass.IN, 3600, "ns.example.com.", "hostmaster.example.com.", 2023010101, 7200, 3600, 1209600, 3600)'}], 'expected': 'No exception; zone.SOA is set to initialSOA.', 'description': 'Set up the zone with an initial SOA record.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'r', 'value': 'newSOA = new SOARecord(Name.fromString("example.com."), DClass.IN, 3600, "ns2.example.com.", "hostmaster.example.com.", 2024010101, 7200, 3600, 1209600, 3600)'}], 'expected': 'No exception; the previous SOA record is removed from its RRset, zone.SOA is updated to newSOA, and the RRset now contains only newSOA.', 'description': "Adding a second SOA record with the same zone origin should replace the existing SOA in the RRset and update the Zone's SOA field."}]}]
